{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-26", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919418, "segment_id": "WreI3Obbs1", "segment_broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Brian Williams (Mississippi)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919418, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-26", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919418, "segment_id": "qbLz2N26w3", "segment_broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "segment_title": "Decision 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / Debate", "segment_description": "(Oxford, Mississippi: Brian Williams) Tonight\u2019s presidential debate between Senators John McCain and Barack Obama introduced.  \n\n(Oxford, Mississippi: Andrea Mitchell) The debate previewed; details given of McCain's decision to attend after saying he wouldn\u2019t without an economic bailout deal; scenes shown from the University of Mississippi and of the candidates in primary debates; McCain campaign statement quoted. [On the plane, OBAMA \u2013 comments on going to Mississippi despite not knowing whether McCain will show up.] [Representative Roy BLUNT\u2020- says McCain was helpful.] [Obama chief strategist David AXELROD\u2020- says we had some political theater.] [Political analyst Mike MURPHY\u2020, Democratic debate coach Robert SHRUM\u2020- explain what each candidate needs to do.]  \n\n(Oxford, Mississippi: Brian Williams, Chuck Todd) McCain's reversal of his decision and debate strategies for the candidates discussed. ", "segment_duration": 310, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919419, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-26", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919418, "segment_id": "npPjgv1wr1", "segment_broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "segment_title": "Economy: Bailout Deal / Washington Mutual", "segment_description": "(Oxford, Mississippi: Brian Williams) Report introduced.   (Capitol: Tom Costello) The ongoing negotiations over a bailout deal for the financial industry featured; details given of opposition from conservative Republicans and their alternative plan. [Representative John BOEHNER&#134;- accuses the White House of ganging up on him.] [President BUSH \u2013 says the legislative process is sometimes not very pretty.] [Representative Eric CANTOR&#134;- comments on reducing the burden on taxpayers.] [Senator Christopher DODD&#134;- explains why Republicans were not invited to a bipartisan meeting.] [Senator Harry REID \u2013 says we need the House Republicans to join us.]   (Oxford, Mississippi: Brian Williams) An internal report indicating the SEC mishandled the banking crisis, including the collapse of Bear Stearns, noted.    (Los Angeles: George Lewis) The largest-ever bank failure in the US with Washington Mutual seized by the government and bought by JPMorgan Chase featured; statistics on branch locations and assets cited. [WaMu customers Oliver PEARCE&#134;, Jeannie RILEY&#135;, Betty SERLIN&#135;- react.] [FDIC chairman Sheila BAIR&#134;- says we have protected taxpayers, depositors and the deposit insurance fund.] [CNBC\u2019s David FABER&#134;- comments on the JPMorgan deal.]   (Oxford, Mississippi: Brian Williams) Discussions between Wachovia bank and potential buyers reported. ", "segment_duration": 350, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63360.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919420, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-26", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919418, "segment_id": "Se7PQz1sSW", "segment_broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "segment_title": "Gasoline Shortage / Southeast", "segment_description": "(Oxford, Mississippi: Brian Williams) Report introduced.  \n\n(Charlotte, North Carolina: Michelle Kosinski) The gasoline shortages in the Southeast due to refineries being closed by Hurricanes Gustav and Ike updated; scenes shown of lines at stations in Charlotte, North Carolina. ", "segment_duration": 120, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63710.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919421, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "uinqBnL6eZ", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-26", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 9194